; Install-script policy (npm >= 11.16, RFC npm/rfcs#868).
;
; npm resolves the effective policy from, highest precedence first:
;   1. --allow-scripts on the CLI  (an ERROR for project-scoped install/ci --
;      never pass it in CI)
;   2. the root package.json "allowScripts" field
;   3. this .npmrc
;
; The root package.json deliberately does not declare "allowScripts", so this
; file is the project's policy. If one is ever added there, npm ignores this
; layer entirely and logs a warning -- move the list, don't duplicate it.
;
; Why it is needed: better-sqlite3 is a native module and compiles (or fetches
; a prebuild) in its install script; esbuild and @swc/core unpack platform
; binaries; msgpackr-extract selects or builds its optional native accelerator.
;
; strict-allow-scripts turns every install script outside this reviewed list
; into a hard failure. Only bare package names are permitted here; semver ranges
; are rejected by npm (exact versions joined by "||" are the alternative).
; fsevents is macOS-only and inert on CI; it is listed so contributor machines
; match CI exactly.
strict-allow-scripts=true
allow-scripts=@swc/core,better-sqlite3,esbuild,fsevents,msgpackr-extract
